# Project Vision: Trip2Talk V4
# File: .cursorrules — place at project root
# Chapter99 Solutions | Sydney, Australia

## 1. Goal
Build a premium PWA booking platform for Trip2Talk —
photography tours led by Thai-speaking guides departing
from Sydney International Airport. Target: Thai-speaking
customers in Australia seeking guided photography travel.

Business details:
- Name: Trip2Talk
- Domain: trip2talk.com.au
- Leader: พี่แสน (Saen) — professional photographer
- Co-host: Monsicha / Ploy
- Departure: Sydney International Airport (all multi-day tours)
- Language: Thai primary, English secondary
- Business rule: ALWAYS use "ทริป" NEVER "ทัวร์"

## 2. Technical Stack
- Framework: React + TypeScript + Vite + PWA (vite-plugin-pwa)
- Database: Supabase (project: rvcwprxnqwscgjusmjvj)
- Supabase URL: https://rvcwprxnqwscgjusmjvj.supabase.co
- Hosting: Vercel (trip2talk.com.au)
- Repo: github.com/chapter99info-cell/trip2talk-v4
- Styling: Tailwind CSS
- Fonts: Fraunces (headings), Inter (body)
- Animation: Framer Motion
- Google Sheets: trip details read from "Trip info" tab
- GAS Web App: https://script.google.com/macros/s/AKfycbzssDNtpEwb2l2V0foX0gAdkO20ucRVI3GJlbG9erhJrp1Q7D-XSNbv-OdSgC-LEU7m3g/exec

## 3. Design System
Dark luxury Gold theme — NON-NEGOTIABLE:
- Background primary: #0A0A0A (near black)
- Background card: #111111 / #1A1A1A
- Gold accent: #C9A84C (warm gold)
- Gold light: #E8C97A
- Text primary: #FFFFFF
- Text muted: #888888 / #999999
- Border: #2A2A2A
- Success: #22C55E
- Error: #EF4444

Typography:
- Headings: Fraunces (serif, italic for hero)
- Body: Inter (sans-serif)
- Thai text: Noto Sans Thai
- Price display: Fraunces bold, large

Spacing: Tailwind defaults, generous padding (p-6 minimum on cards)

## 4. Supabase Architecture (CRITICAL — DO NOT BREAK)

Tables (23 total):
tours, tour_bookings, trip_bookings, crm_clients,
staff_profiles, expenses, gallery, gallery_posts,
trip_gallery, client_guide_content, client_reviews,
client_waivers, waivers, reviews, staff_commission_ledger,
packing_items, emergency_contacts, offline_map_pins,
tour_itinerary, tour_itinerary_blocks, tour_itinerary_days,
tour_map_pins, gallery_likes

RLS status: ENABLED on all tables (do not disable)

Booking flow (ATOMIC — never break this):
1. Frontend calls RPC: claim_seat_and_book (SECURITY DEFINER)
2. RPC atomically: decrements seats + creates tour_booking row
3. No direct UPDATE on seats from frontend — RPC only
4. Overbooking prevention: hard-block when seats = 0

Trip data source:
- Google Sheet "Trip info" tab (NOT "Trips_Data")
- 20-column Title-Case headers, data from row 2
- Read via GAS Web App URL above
- Supabase = single source of truth for seats

## 5. PIN System (4 access levels)
- 1111 = Staff (read bookings, view dashboard)
- 4444 = Co-Host (adjust seats ±, view bookings)
- 9999 = Owner (full access, all features)
- 3501 = Platform (super admin, all Chapter99 data)

PIN verified via: verify_pin RPC (client-side, NOT Supabase Auth)
Dashboard policies named: *_dashboard_anon_* (hybrid RLS)

## 6. The 8 Trips
trip_code: TAS-3D2N, MEL-4D3N, ULU-4D3N, NZ-6D5N,
           TAS-LH-4D3N, KIA-1DAY, CAN-2D1N, SYD-1DAY

NZ-6D5N = FLAGSHIP (styled larger, price: A$2,350)
Meeting point: Sydney International Airport (all multi-day)

Storage bucket: "portfolio"
Note: ULU folder misspelled "Ulruru" — use as-is
Hobart images: "Tasmania/Hobart" folder

## 7. Payment Rules
- Deposit: A$100 (book now, pay later)
- Installment 1: equal amount, 30 days post-booking
- Installment 2: equal amount, 20 days before departure
- No full payment upfront required

## 8. Security Rules (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
- Supabase anon key in .env only (VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY)
- service_role key NEVER in frontend — Edge Functions only
- RLS enabled on ALL tables always
- Google Sheet: Restricted access only (not public edit)
- No sensitive booking data in console.log

## 9. SEO + AI Friendly
- Title: "Trip2Talk | ทริปถ่ายภาพสำหรับคนไทยในออสเตรเลีย"
- Schema: TouristTrip + LocalBusiness
- FAQ: ออกเดินทางจากไหน / ราคาเท่าไหร่ / จองยังไง
- Language: Thai (th-AU) as primary

## 10. Development Workflow
- Read Google Sheet via GAS before any trip data change
- Always test booking flow with claim_seat_and_book RPC
- Check seats in Supabase directly to verify atomic lock
- New features: test on mobile (iPhone) first
- git commit: "feat: [thai description]"
- Use Sonnet — NEVER Opus unless architecture/RPC work
- NEVER Multitask
- Push to GitHub = auto deploy to Vercel

## 11. Current Task
[REPLACE THIS: Describe the specific feature to build]
Example: "Fix Co-Host Terminal ± seat controls"
Example: "Add Hobart gallery slideshow"
Example: "Fix GAS web app to read Trip info tab"
Example: "Send Resend confirmation email after booking"

## 12. Constraints
- "ทริป" always — NEVER "ทัวร์" in any text
- Seat count always visible on booking page
- Hard-block booking when seats = 0 (no exceptions)
- Trips without date = unbookable (date gate enforced)
- Dark theme always — no light mode
- Load time: under 3 seconds even with gallery images
- Fraunces headings on all hero and tour title sections
